Chapter: AnnotSeed

  cites Works chapter RepoProtocolPersist
  cites Works chapter Annotation
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 How to run it, and it WRITES, so give it a copy:

   build/compile.ps1 -Src docs/Probes/annotation-mark-seed.codex
     -Out seed.cdx -Kernel seed/Codex.cdx -Log seed.log
   Copy-Item seed/Codex.img annot.img
   tools/codex-vm.exe -kernel seed.cdx -output seed.txt -mem 3072
     -headless -disk annot.img

 Then `build/desk.ps1 -Force -Disk annot.img` and open SRC/NAME.COD: line 9
 carries the gutter mark. The same desk on an unseeded `seed/Codex.img` is
 the control and shows none.

 Writes one annotation onto the attached medium's fact partition so the Edit
 pane has something to mark. The target is a definition that really exists in
 SRC/NAME.COD on seed/Codex.img: chapter `Name`, path `make-name`.

 The second annotation targets a name that is NOT in that file, which is the
 control the arm needs: if a mark appears for it, the match is not doing what
 it says.

Section: Entry

  seed-target : Text, Text -> AnnotationTarget
  seed-target (ch) (path) = AnnotationTarget { chapter = ch, path = path }

 `create-annotation` takes the AUTHOR before the body. Written the other way
 round the store is still valid and the pane still marks the right line, so
 nothing fails; the bubble is what shows it, printing the body where the name
 belongs. Any test that only counts annotations passes either way.

  ann-hit : Annotation = create-annotation (seed-target "Name" "make-name") Invariant "val" "make-name is the only constructor" 2000

  ann-miss : Annotation = create-annotation (seed-target "Name" "no-such-def") Invariant "val" "targets nothing in this file" 2100

  opening : [Device.Block, Console.Write] Nothing = act
    let s0 = disk-init
    in let s1 = repo-persist-save-annotation s0 ann-hit 2000
    in let s2 = repo-persist-save-annotation s1 ann-miss 2100
    in let back = disk-load
    in let all = repo-persist-load-all-annotations back
    in act
      print-line-uni ("annotations written and read back: " & show (list-length all))
      print-line-uni ("first target: " & show-target all 0)
      print-line-uni ("second target: " & show-target all 1)
    end
  end

  show-target : List Annotation, Integer -> Text
  show-target (anns) (i) =
    if i >= list-length anns then "<none>"
    else let a = list-at anns i
    in (a.target).chapter & "::" & (a.target).path
